// Title: a FinalValues program that keeps one async call in flight (an accept
// nobody connects to) is Timeout(Deadline) in every mode, so the oracle compares
// none of its values: the settle loop waits REPLY_WAIT (10 s, unscaled) inside a
// run deadline of 10 s (check/run) or 3 s (campaigns).
// Command: graphix-fuzz check fuzz-main-aux-pending-reply-timeout.gx
//          graphix-fuzz run fuzz-main-aux-pending-reply-timeout.gx
// Expected: each engine a trace [0:5] (the value is deterministic: a constant at
//   init), compared at final strength.
// Observed: run: every mode "Timeout(Deadline)"; check (50 s): "AGREE (contained)".
//   A JIT that answered 6 here would agree.
// Control: the same program with `let z = throttle(i64:1);` added (an Excluded
//   marker, which skips the FinalValues settle loop) runs Trace([0:5]) at once in
//   every mode, so the loop's wait_replies is what times out.
let l = sys::tcp::listen("127.0.0.1:0")$;
let c = sys::tcp::accept(l, null);
let v = i64:5;
v
